.TH DOTDOC 1 "August 2026" "dotdoc @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotdoc \- scan a directory tree for symbolic-link findings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotdoc
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotdoc
scans a directory tree recursively and reports broken and absolute symbolic links.

Dotfiles are the primary use case, but an explicitly specified
.IR PATH
may be any directory tree.

Without
.IR PATH ,
the directory
.B $HOME/dotfiles
is scanned.

With
.IR PATH ,
the specified directory tree is scanned.

Directory symbolic links are inspected as symbolic links but their target
directories are not traversed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Diagnostic findings are written to standard output.

Invocation and filesystem errors are written to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan completed successfully with no findings.
.TP
.B 1
The scan completed successfully and diagnostic findings were found.
This does not indicate program failure.
.TP
.B 2
An invocation, filesystem, or scan error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan the default dotfiles tree:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dotdoc
.RE
.fi
.PP
Scan a specific directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dotdoc ~/dotfiles
.RE
.fi
.PP
Display help:
.PP
.nf
.RS
dotdoc --help
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $HOME/dotfiles
Default scan root when no
.I PATH
is specified.
